n><span style=\"color:#606\">Flight</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Connections</span><span style=\"color:#000\">     </span><span style=\"color:#066\">479</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#066\">33</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Online</span><span style=\"color:#660\">/</span><span style=\"color:#606\">Navigational</span><span style=\"color:#000\">          </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Flight</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Fares</span><span style=\"color:#000\">     </span><span style=\"color:#066\">648</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#066\">34</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Online</span><span style=\"color:#660\">/</span><span style=\"color:#606\">Navigational</span><span style=\"color:#000\">        </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Flight</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Options</span><span style=\"color:#000\">    </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1176</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">...</span></pre></div></code></div><br>And from here, I create a stacked column plot. Each column is assigned an area and within each area you have the different categories:<br><br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">a </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> hPlot</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#606\">Listens</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">~</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Areas</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> <br>                 data </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#606\">CatplotData</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> <br>                 type </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;column&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> <br>                 </span><span style=\"color:#008\">group</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;Categories&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> <br>                 </span><span style=\"color:#008\">group</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">na </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;NA\\&#39;s&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span></div></code></div><br>Add any other parameters to customize your plot ...<br><br>Then, this is my JS code to track when the user clicks on any of the categories on any of the areas:<br><br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">a$plotOptions</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">column </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> list</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">stacking </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;normal&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> <br>                                  cursor </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;pointer&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> <br>                                  point </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> list</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">events </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> list</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">click </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> <br>                                                             </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;#! function() { <br>                                                             Shiny.onInputChange(&#39;click&#39;, {                                            <br>                                                             topic: <a href=\"http://this.name\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://this.name&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792397954963000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1rfNYIoy-Qn_03uzzViaUP\">this.name</a> + &#39;-&#39; + <a href=\"http://this.series.name\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://this.series.name&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792397954963000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2xRSBVjomMz0vDLB95V1n8\">this.series.name</a><br>                                                           })<br>                                                           } !#&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))))</span></div></code></div><br>In the R code I just:<br><br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">observe </span><span style=\"color:#660\">({</span><span style=\"color:#000\">  <br>   input$click$topic<br>   <br>   </span><span style=\"color:#800\">#add whatever logic you want execute</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">})</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br> <br></span></div></code></div><br>I hope this helps.<br><br>Carlos</div>"
